     hhaasshhffiilltteerr _f_i_l_t_e_r_-_s_p_e_c_i_f_i_c_a_t_i_o_n
     ffiilltteerr _i_d_x _f_i_l_t_e_r_-_s_p_e_c_i_f_i_c_a_t_i_o_n
     Program a filter.

     TCAM filters: The number of available filters is in dev.<nexus>.<in‐
     stance>.nfilters.  _i_d_x must be an unused index between 0 and nfilters -
     1.  IPv6 filters consume 4 consecutive entries on T4/T5 and 2 on T6 and
     _i_d_x must be aligned to 4 or 2 in this case.

     Hash filters:  These reside in the card's memory instead of its TCAM and
     are enabled with a special configuration file that is selected with
     hhww..ccxxggbbee..ccoonnffiigg__ffiillee==""hhaasshhffiilltteerr"" in loader.conf.  There are at least
     half a million filters available with the sample config shipped with the
     driver.  Note that the hardware selects the index for a hashfilter and
     this index is displayed when the filter is created.  Hash and TCAM fil‐
     ters can be used together.

     _f_i_l_t_e_r_-_s_p_e_c_i_f_i_c_a_t_i_o_n consists of one or more matches (see Usage in the
     table above) to try against an incoming frame, an action to perform when
     all matches succeed, and some additional operational parameters.  Hash‐
     filters require an exact value for the 5-tuple (sip, dip, sport, dport,
     proto) and for any other match-criteria listed in "hashfilter mode".
     Possible filter actions are ddrroopp, ppaassss, or sswwiittcchh.

           Operational parameters that can be used with all filters:
           hhiittccnnttss    Count filter hits: 0 or 1 (default).
           pprriioo       Filter has priority over active and server regions of
                      TCAM: 0 (default) or 1.

           Operational parameters that can be used with filters with aaccttiioonn
           ppaassss:
           qquueeuuee      Context id of an ingress queue to which to deliver the
                      packet.  The context id is available in
                      _d_e_v_._c_x_g_b_e_._%_d_._r_x_q_._%_d_._c_n_t_x_t___i_d.  By default, packets that
                      hit a filter with action pass are delivered based on
                      their RSS hash as usual.  Use this to steer them to a
                      particular queue.
           rrppttttiidd     Report the filter tid instead of the RSS hash in the rx
                      descriptor.  0 (default) or 1.
           ttccbbhhaasshh    Select TCB hash information in rx descriptor.  0 (de‐
                      fault) or 1

           Operational parameters that can be used with filters with aaccttiioonn
           sswwiittcchh:
           eeppoorrtt      Egress port number on which to send the packet matching
                      the filter.  0 to dev.<nexus>.<instance>.nports - 1.
           ddmmaacc       Replace packet destination MAC address with the one pro‐
                      vided before switching it out of eport.
           ssmmaacc       Replace packet source MAC address with the one provided
                      before switching it out of eport.
           sswwaappmmaacc    Swap packet source and destination MAC addresses before
                      switching it out of eport.
           vvllaann       Insert, remove, or rewrite the VLAN tag before switching
                      the packet out of eport.  nnoonnee removes the tag, ==_t_a_g re‐
                      places the existing tag with the one provided, and ++_t_a_g
                      inserts the given tag into the frame.
           nnaatt        Specify the desired NAT mode. Valid NAT modes values
                      are:
                      ddiipp         Perform NAT on destination IP.
                      ddiipp--ddpp      Perform NAT on destination IP, destination
                                  port.
